  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/6E6B/marshal/issues</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/6E6B/marshal</url>
  <description>
    <p>
      Marshal is a GNOME application for controlling servers that use the
      Model Context Protocol (MCP).
    </p>
    <p>With Marshal you can:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Start and stop MCP servers</li>
      <li>Inspect a server’s tools and logs</li>
      <li>Install server configuration into client programs</li>
      <li>Give remote access with OpenAI or ngrok</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Stdio servers, tunnel clients, and agent CLIs run on the host. Install
      those tools on your system before using them from Marshal.
    </p>
  </description>
